1
00:04:51,428 --> 00:04:57,428
Every saga has a beginning.

2
00:09:42,857 --> 00:09:48,857
Star Wars: Episode I - The Phantom Menace is a adventure, action,
science fiction film directed by George Lucas.

3
00:14:34,285 --> 00:14:40,285
Anakin Skywalker, a young slave strong with the
Force, is discovered on Tatooine.

4
00:19:25,714 --> 00:19:31,714
Meanwhile, the evil Sith have returned, enacting
their plot for revenge against the Jedi.

5
00:24:17,142 --> 00:24:23,142
Qui-Gon Jinn, played by Liam Neeson.

6
00:29:08,571 --> 00:29:14,571
Obi-Wan Kenobi, played by Ewan McGregor.

7
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Padmé Amidala, played by Natalie Portman.

8
00:38:51,428 --> 00:38:57,428
Anakin Skywalker, played by Jake Lloyd.

9
00:43:42,857 --> 00:43:48,857
Senator Palpatine, played by Ian McDiarmid.

10
00:48:34,285 --> 00:48:40,285
Shmi Skywalker, played by Pernilla August.

11
00:53:25,714 --> 00:53:31,714
Star Wars Episode I: Racer is a 1999 racing video game
developed and published by LucasArts.

12
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
It is based on the podracing sequence in the film Star
Wars: Episode I – The Phantom Menace.

13
01:03:08,571 --> 01:03:14,571
The game features all of the racers and race course
on Tatooine from The Phantom Menace.

14
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
It adds several new courses, on Tatooine and various planets.

15
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
The game has several single player modes, including a tournament mode.

16
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
The format of multiplayer mode varies by platform.

17
01:22:34,285 --> 01:22:40,285
Jake Lloyd and Lewis MacLeod, who portrayed Anakin Skywalker and Sebulba in
The Phantom Menace, reprise their film roles in the game.

18
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
Episode I: Racer received generally positive reviews from critics.

19
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
Several major media outlets listed it as one of the top Star Wars video games.

20
01:37:08,571 --> 01:37:14,571
As of 2011, the game holds the Guinness record as the best-selling sci-fi racing game, with
worldwide sales of 3.12 million units, followed by series like Wipeout and F-Zero.

21
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
Two podracing games were released later.

22
01:46:51,428 --> 01:46:57,428
Star Wars: Racer Arcade, an arcade game featuring many similar
tracks and characters, was released in 2000.

23
01:51:42,857 --> 01:51:48,857
A sequel, Star Wars Racer Revenge was released in 2002 for the PlayStation 2.

24
01:56:34,285 --> 01:56:40,285
Twenty years after the release of the game, it received an HD
re-release for Nintendo Switch and PlayStation 4 in June 2020.

25
02:01:25,714 --> 02:01:31,714
It was later released on Xbox One in October 2020.

26
02:06:17,142 --> 02:06:23,142
The film explores themes of galaxy, senate, taskmaster, prophecy, queen.

27
02:11:08,571 --> 02:11:14,571
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
